{* The settings dialog itself: the trigger, the tab shell and the actions row.

	<dialog> rather than a hand-rolled overlay: it brings the backdrop, focus trapping,
	top-layer stacking and escape-to-close with it, and needs no library. The buttons are
	wired up by src/Assets/javascript/settings-dialog.js.
*}
{parameters
	\AdminerDesktop $desktop,
	\Desktop\Shortcuts\Shortcuts $shortcuts
}
<button type="button" id="desktop-gear" data-dialog="desktop-settings" title="{$desktop->t('settings.title')}" data-shortcut="{$shortcuts->settings()}">&#9881;</button>

{* Not light-dismissed: a stray click beside a dialog this large is too easy. Guarded, so Escape and
	the × ask before throwing edits away (javascript/modal.js). Focus lands on the dialog itself
	rather than on the checked tab, so opening it with the mouse does not ring the tab. *}
{embed '../Assets/modal.latte', id: 'desktop-settings', lightDismiss: false, guard: true, focusSelf: true, labelledBy: 'desktop-settings-title'}
	{* desktop_settings, which tells handlePost() this is a save, comes with the panels. *}
	{block hidden}
		{input_token()|noescape}
	{/block}

	{* Tabs are hidden radios plus :has() in the stylesheet: no JS, and a checked radio is
		also the state, so nothing has to be restored when the dialog reopens. A screen reader
		hears a radio group of four, which is what it is — arrows move between them natively,
		where the ARIA tab pattern would need a roving tabindex in script to do the same. They
		carry no value, so whichever is checked posts the same desktop_tab=on, and switching tabs
		is not an unsaved change to the guard. *}
	{block header}
		<h2 id="desktop-settings-title">{$desktop->t('settings.title')}</h2>
		<div id="desktop-tabs">
			<input type="radio" name="desktop_tab" id="desktop-tab-themes" checked>
			<label for="desktop-tab-themes">{$desktop->t('settings.tab_theme')}</label>
			<input type="radio" name="desktop_tab" id="desktop-tab-plugins">
			<label for="desktop-tab-plugins">{$desktop->t('settings.tab_plugins')}</label>
			<input type="radio" name="desktop_tab" id="desktop-tab-mcp">
			<label for="desktop-tab-mcp">{$desktop->t('settings.tab_mcp')}</label>
			<input type="radio" name="desktop_tab" id="desktop-tab-shortcuts">
			<label for="desktop-tab-shortcuts">{$desktop->t('settings.tab_shortcuts')}</label>
		</div>
	{/block}

	{* Empty until the dialog first opens: modal.js fetches the panels (settings-panels.latte) from
		data-src, so a page that never opens settings never renders them. On this page's connection
		(adminer's ME), so a link in a panel can stay on it: the panels are answered before ME exists. *}
	{block body}
		<div id="desktop-panels" data-src="{\Adminer\ME}desktop_settings_panels=1">
			<p class="error" hidden data-load-failed>{$desktop->t('settings.load_failed')}</p>
		</div>
	{/block}

	{block footer}
		{* Its own submit button, named: a named submit posts its own name, so nothing here
			needs a hidden field or a line of script to say which button was pressed. Left of
			the others, away from the one people press without reading. *}
		<button type="submit" name="desktop_reset" value="1" id="desktop-reset" class="ad-danger"
			data-confirm="{$desktop->t('settings.reset_confirm')}">{$desktop->t('settings.reset')}</button>
		<button type="submit" id="desktop-save" class="ad-primary">{$desktop->t('settings.save')}</button>
	{/block}
{/embed}

{* The question every guarded modal asks before a changed form is thrown away (javascript/modal.js).
	Here because this template is printed on every page, and the settings dialog is guarded too.
	Keep editing is the safe answer, so it has the focus; Escape answers it too. *}
{embed '../Assets/modal.latte', id: 'ad-discard', class: 'ad-confirm-dialog', form: false, labelledBy: 'ad-discard-title'}
	{block header}<h2 id="ad-discard-title">{$desktop->t('connections.discard_title')}</h2>{/block}
	{block body}{$desktop->t('connections.discard_text')}{/block}
	{block footer}
		<button type="button" data-close autofocus>{$desktop->t('connections.keep_editing')}</button>
		<button type="button" class="ad-destructive" data-discard>{$desktop->t('connections.discard')}</button>
	{/block}
{/embed}
